# Line endings that must hold on every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says. Everything that a
# Linux container, a Linux server, make or a POSIX shell reads stays LF: one CR at a line's end
# breaks a shebang, a heredoc, a Makefile recipe, a Caddyfile directive, or an Ansible template
# rendered on the host. Everything else follows the checkout's own settings.

# Whole trees that only ever run on Linux. text=auto still leaves binaries alone.
deploy/** text=auto eol=lf
infra/** text=auto eol=lf
.github/** text=auto eol=lf

# The Makefile, shell scripts, and the templates Ansible renders.
Makefile text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.j2 text eol=lf
# Run by its shebang as well as by `python manage.py`.
manage.py text eol=lf

# Container builds.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf

# Configs mounted into containers, compose files and the rest.
*.conf text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# PowerShell, for Windows.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never converted or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.onnx binary
*.npz binary
